 [docker-build] Don't link files from outside the project directory (e.g. `src/Shared/`) without adding a `COPY` instruction for that shared directory in all relevant Dockerfiles — `dotnet publish` will fail inside Docker with `CS2001: Source file could not be found`. (cause: MSBuild linked files outside the project root)
 [testing] Don't change the visibility of a public API class without manually updating its `public-api-baseline.txt` (or equivalent snapshot file) — Public API Snapshot Tests will fail with "Strings differ" because the actual API shrank relative to the baseline. (cause: API snapshot strictness)
 [architecture] Don't reference a high-level domain module (like Approvals) from a generic engine (like AuditOutbox) just to reuse a small utility class — this creates an inverted boundary dependency. Use MSBuild file linking or accept duplication instead. (cause: generic engines depending on specific domains)
+[test-refactoring] Don't assume metric counter semantics survive a monolith→executor split — when a monolith splits into separate executors, counters previously incremented inline may no longer fire if the responsible executor is short-circuited. Update tests to reflect the new architecture rather than forcing old counter increments. (cause: DecideExecutor drops silently on null decision, so invalidArguments counter in ValidateExecutor was never reached)
